id=a52sxq_resolution_scaling
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Screen resolution keeps the physical size and position of the UI
author=kusti420
description=Display > Screen resolution (unica/mods/settings, HD+ / 540p) renders at a lower size through WindowManager's forced size + density. WindowManager already rescales the camera cutout and the rounded corners for a forced size, and dp follows the density, but it left the display's physical dpi (DisplayInfo.physicalXDpi/YDpi -> DisplayMetrics.xdpi/ydpi) at the native value. Everything that converts millimetres to pixels then lands 1.5x / 2x too big: mm resources and Samsung's own geometry code, e.g. SystemUI DeviceState.setInDisplayFingerprintSensorPosition() (fingerprint icon and touch area from the sensor position in mm). Samsung's multi-resolution phones switch a real display mode, where the dpi comes with the mode. This patch makes DisplayContent.updateBaseDisplayMetrics() derive the physical dpi from the real panel dpi and the forced size (dpi x forced width / native width; unchanged at native resolution). The status bar pixel dimens of the target overlay (target/a52sxq/overlay/values/dimens.xml) are written in mm for the same reason.
